---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Colchester, CT's 1790 Revolutionary War Landmark"
  description="Tour the story and ongoing restoration of the General Henry Champion House, a 1790 National Register landmark in Colchester, Connecticut, with deep ties to the Revolutionary War and the Champion family."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/home-front-summer.webp"
      alt="Front elevation of the General Henry Champion House in summer, with patriotic bunting, a cannon, and the barn visible"
      class="h-[70vh] w-full object-cover"
      width="1200"
      height="900"
      fetchpriority="high"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/85 via-black/45 to-black/5"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-end">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 pb-16 text-white [text-shadow:0_2px_10px_rgba(0,0,0,0.55)]">
        <h1 class="max-w-2xl text-4xl md:text-5xl">The General Henry Champion House</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg text-white/90">
          A Revolutionary-era landmark, under restoration, and open to your support.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6">
          <a href="/history" class="text-base font-medium text-white underline decoration-[var(--color-stone)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-stone)]">
            Read the House's History &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mission -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <p class="eyebrow text-[var(--color-brick)]">Our Mission</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]">
      The General Henry Champion Trust is dedicated to preserving, restoring, and protecting the 1790
      General Henry Champion House &mdash; an architecturally significant Federal-period home listed on
      the State and National Registers of Historic Places. Our work restores the house and its historic
      landscape to their documented original appearance, while sharing the story of the Champion family
      and Connecticut's Revolutionary-era history with the public.
    </p>
    <a href="/donate" class="btn-secondary mt-6 inline-block">Read our full mission &rarr;</a>
  </section>

  <!-- Historical highlight -->
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 px-6 py-16 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="md:order-2">
        <img
          src="/images/gallery/archival-photo-front-topiary.webp"
          alt="Archival black-and-white photograph of the General Henry Champion House"
          class="h-80 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm"
          data-lightbox
          width="206"
          height="211"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="md:order-1">
        <p class="eyebrow text-[var(--color-brick)]">A Revolutionary Story</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl">The Winter the Champions Fed an Army</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          In the brutal winter of 1777&ndash;78, Colonel Henry Champion &mdash; the Revolutionary War
          officer who would build this house a decade later &mdash; personally drove a herd of cattle 300
          miles to reach Washington's starving army at Valley Forge. Purchased at great expense, the cattle
          were eaten by the troops within five days of arrival.
        </p>
        <a href="/history#colonel" class="btn-secondary mt-6 inline-block">Read the Full History &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Restoration callout -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--color-parchment)]">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 px-6 py-16 md:grid-cols-2">
      <img
        src="/images/restoration-roof-aerial-2025-thumb.webp"
        data-full-src="/images/restoration-roof-aerial-2025.webp"
        alt="Aerial view of the house's roof mid-repair"
        class="h-80 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm"
        data-lightbox
        width="900"
        height="600"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl">A House in the Making, Again</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          The Champion House sat vacant and deteriorating for years before the Trust acquired it. Today,
          restoration is underway &mdash; starting with the roof &mdash; to bring the house back to the
          condition it deserves. Follow along as the work progresses.
        </p>
        <a href="/restoration" class="btn-primary mt-6">See Restoration Progress &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quick links -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
      <a href="/history" class="group block">
        <h3 class="text-xl group-hover:text-[var(--color-brick)]">History</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          Two Champions, a Revolutionary War, and a house built to last. Learn the story behind the name.
        </p>
        <span class="btn-secondary mt-4 inline-block text-sm">Read More</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/restoration" class="group block">
        <h3 class="text-xl group-hover:text-[var(--color-brick)]">Restoration Progress</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          Before, during, and after &mdash; an honest record of the work as it happens.
        </p>
        <span class="btn-secondary mt-4 inline-block text-sm">See Progress</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/visit" class="group block">
        <h3 class="text-xl group-hover:text-[var(--color-brick)]">Visit / Contact</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          Have a question, a document, or an old photograph of the house? We'd love to hear from you.
        </p>
        <span class="btn-secondary mt-4 inline-block text-sm">Get in Touch</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Donation banner -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-cream)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Help Us Bring the House Back</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-white/80">
        Every gift goes directly toward preserving a piece of Connecticut's Revolutionary-era history for
        future generations. The General Henry Champion Trust is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization; your
        donation is tax-deductible.
      </p>
      <a href="/donate" class="btn-primary mt-8 shadow-lg shadow-black/50 ring-1 ring-white/15">Support the Restoration</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
